{
 "_note": "THE ATTRIBUTE TABLE, folded. Every `<scroll>` attribute resolves through ONE total function: no input throws, no unrecognised word fails a build, and every unknown value falls back to the documented default — the same law the keyboard corpus states for its mode word, and for the same reason (these values come from authored markup and a dashboard, not from a schema). Notes on the three that are not obvious. `bounces` is TRISTATE: unset is not `true`, it means the PLATFORM decides, and collapsing that to a boolean is how a framework ends up overriding iOS's default bounce on every scroll view it renders. `paging` and `snap` are one setting with two spellings, so paging resolves to snap=\"page\" and outranks a declared snap word rather than silently fighting it. `contentInset` follows CSS edge shorthand exactly (1/2/3/4 values), because an author who has written CSS already knows it. Defaults worth stating: indicators on, keyboardDismiss `interactive` (the messaging-app idiom, and the one almost nobody implements), overscroll `auto`, threshold 0.",
 "cases": [
